# Line endings.
#
# Git stores every text file with LF in the repository. On checkout the working
# tree follows core.autocrlf, so Windows keeps CRLF while the stored blobs stay
# LF. Without this rule a file edited with mixed or LF endings shows up as
# "modified" even though its content is identical.
* text=auto

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted or word-diffed.
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.otf binary
*.ttf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
